## Legend Auto-Generation

The component automatically generates legend items based on the data:

1. **Detects series count** from data (counts unique series names in canonical format, or checks value1/value2/value3 in legacy format; capped at 3)
2. **Creates legend items** for each series with categorical colors (`categorical/bold/{1–3}`)
3. **Uses series labels** from canonical format's series names, or falls back to `chartLegendConfig` (series1Label, series2Label, series3Label)
4. **Can be overridden** with `chartLegendConfig.items` prop for custom legends

## Height Behavior

The `height` prop controls the **total chart height**, not just the bar group. The VerticalMultiBarGroup automatically stretches to fill the remaining space after header, legend, DataDisplay, and footer.

### How It Works

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ChartHeader (natural height)            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ChartLegend (natural height)            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ DataDisplay (natural height, optional)  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                         │
│ VerticalMultiBarGroup (flex: 1, fills)  │
│                                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ChartFooter (natural height)            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
       ↑                                ↑
       └────── Total height prop ───────┘
```

### Usage Examples

```tsx
// Fixed 500px chart - bar group fills remaining space
<VerticalMultiBarChart
  data={data}
  height={500}
  chartHeader={true}
  chartFooter={true}
/>

// Compact 280px chart for dashboards
<VerticalMultiBarChart
  data={data}
  height={280}
  chartHeader={true}
  chartFooter={false}
  chartLegend={false}
/>

// Bars only - fills full height
<VerticalMultiBarChart
  data={data}
  height={300}
  chartHeader={false}
  chartFooter={false}
  chartLegend={false}
/>
```

### Key Benefits

1. **Predictable sizing**: Chart always respects the specified height
2. **Automatic stretching**: Bar group expands to fill available space
3. **Consistent layouts**: Same chart height regardless of which sections are visible
4. **Responsive-friendly**: Use percentage heights for fluid layouts

## Legend Customization

The `chartLegendConfig` prop supports extensive customization of the legend appearance and behavior.

### New Props (v0.1.0+)

| Prop              | Type                            | Default    | Description                                                                 |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `type`            | `'circle' \| 'dashed' \| 'line'` | `'circle'` | Indicator shape for auto-generated legend items                             |
| `dataHead`        | `boolean`                       | `false`    | Show DataHead blocks below legend labels                                    |
| `dataHeadConfig`  | `object`                        | -          | Configure static DataHead values (lead value, supporting label, etc.)       |
| `size`            | `'XS' \| 'S' \| 'M' \| 'L' \| 'XL'` | -          | Typography size variant for legend items                                    |
| `interactiveDataHead` | `boolean`                   | `false`    | Update DataHead values on bar hover (overrides static values)               |

### Usage Examples

```tsx
// Custom indicator shape
<VerticalMultiBarChart
  data={data}
  chartLegend={true}
  chartLegendConfig={{
    series1Label: 'Product A',
    series2Label: 'Product B',
    type: 'dashed', // Use dashed indicators instead of circles
  }}
/>

// Static DataHead showing series totals
<VerticalMultiBarChart
  data={data}
  chartLegend={true}
  chartLegendConfig={{
    series1Label: 'Revenue',
    series2Label: 'Expenses',
    dataHead: true,
    dataHeadConfig: {
      dataLeadValue: 1234,
      supportingLabelValue: 'Total',
    },
  }}
/>

// Larger legend typography
<VerticalMultiBarChart
  data={data}
  chartLegend={true}
  chartLegendConfig={{
    size: 'L', // Larger legend text
  }}
/>

// Combine static and interactive DataHead
<VerticalMultiBarChart
  data={data}
  chartLegend={true}
  chartLegendConfig={{
    series1Label: 'Product A',
    series2Label: 'Product B',
    type: 'dashed',
    size: 'M',
    dataHead: true,
    dataHeadConfig: {
      dataLeadValue: 1234, // Static total shown by default
      supportingLabelValue: 'Total',
    },
    interactiveDataHead: true, // Updates to per-category value on hover
    formatHoverSupportingLabel: (category, seriesIndex) => `${category}`,
  }}
/>
```

### Static vs Interactive DataHead

- **Static DataHead** (`dataHead` + `dataHeadConfig`): Shows fixed values (e.g., series totals, averages) that don't change
- **Interactive DataHead** (`interactiveDataHead`): Updates values dynamically on bar hover
- **Combined**: Show static values by default, override with hover values when user hovers over bars

This is useful for showing summary statistics (totals, averages) while still providing detailed per-category values on interaction.

## Hover Interaction

The chart supports interactive hover with automatic dimming using design tokens.

### Hover Types

| Type                | Behavior                                                                | Use Case                  |
| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |
| `'group'` (default) | All bars in a category highlight together; other categories dim         | Category-level comparison |
| `'individual'`      | Only the specific hovered bar highlights; all other bars dim            | Individual bar analysis   |
| `'categorical'`     | All bars of the same series across all categories highlight; others dim | Series comparison/legend  |

### Color & Opacity States

| State                         | Color Token               | Opacity            | Description                    |
| ----------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------ |
| **Default** (nothing hovered) | `categorical/bold/{1–6}`  | `1`                | Original vibrant colors        |
| **Highlighted** (hovered)     | `categorical/bold/{1–6}`  | `1`                | Stays vibrant                  |
| **Dimmed** (not hovered)      | `categorical/hover/{1–6}` | `dimOpacity` (0.2) | Muted colors + reduced opacity |

### Transition Tokens

All hover transitions use design tokens from the `hoverAnimation` collection:

- **Easing**: `"easing"` - Cubic-bezier timing function
- **Duration**: `"duration"` - Transition time (e.g., 200ms for "Moderate" mode)
- **Dim Opacity**: `"dimOpacity"` - Opacity for dimmed bars (default: 0.2)

### Callback Data Structure

```typescript
interface VerticalMultiBarHoverData {
  index?: number; // Data point index (category index)
  label?: string; // Category label
  values: number[]; // Values for all bars in the group
  isHovered: boolean; // Whether the group/bar is currently hovered
  barIndex?: number; // 0-based index of hovered bar (individual/categorical modes)
  mouseX?: number; // Mouse X coordinate (clientX)
  mouseY?: number; // Mouse Y coordinate (clientY)
}
```

## Hover Badge

The component supports an optional `DataBadge` that follows the cursor on hover. The content displayed depends on the `hoverType`:

| Hover Type    | Badge Displays | Example Output          |
| ------------- | -------------- | ----------------------- |
| `individual`  | Data value     | `120`, `90`, `150`      |
| `group`       | Category label | `Q1`, `Q2`, `January`   |
| `categorical` | Series name    | `Product A`, `Series 1` |

> **Important:** `hoverType` controls **what** the badge displays. The `hoverBadgeConfig.formatValue` prop only applies to `"individual"` mode — in `"group"` and `"categorical"` modes, the badge always shows the label regardless of any custom formatter. This behavior is enforced by the shared `resolveHoverBadgeFormatter()` utility in `src/utils/resolveHoverBadgeFormatter.ts`.

### Individual Mode - Shows Value

