### With Data Sorting

Sort bars by total segment value via `barGroupConfig.dataSort`:

```tsx
// Descending — highest total bar on the left
<VerticalStackedBarChart
  data={data}
  barGroupConfig={{
    dataSort: "desc",
    yAxis: true,
  }}
/>


// Ascending — lowest total bar on the left
<VerticalStackedBarChart
  data={data}
  barGroupConfig={{
    dataSort: "asc",
  }}
/>

```

`DataSortOrder` values:

| Value        | Behaviour                                        |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `"unsorted"` | Bars appear in the order provided by the dataset |
| `"desc"`     | Highest total first (left) → lowest total last   |
| `"asc"`      | Lowest total first (left) → highest total last   |

Sorting is applied before overflow grouping, so "Others" still works correctly:

```tsx
<VerticalStackedBarChart
  data={manyCategories}
  barGroupConfig={{
    dataSort: "desc",
    categoryLabels: true,
    categoryLabelConfig: {
      overflowType: "grouped",
      othersPosition: "end",
    },
  }}
/>

```

The underlying utility `sortByAccessor()` from `src/utils/dataTransformers.ts` is generic and reusable across all chart types.

